# yggdrasil stack — manual setup

## 0. Make the GHCR packages public

Every image below currently returns "denied" on an anonymous pull (confirmed
via `docker manifest inspect`, 2026-08-25):

- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-web`
- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-api`
- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-orchestrator`
- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-landing`
- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-docusaurus`
- `ghcr.io/yggdrasil-hq/yggdrasil-agent-images`

For each: GitHub → the owning repo → **Packages** (right sidebar) → the
package → **Package settings** → **Change visibility** → Public. (`gh` CLI
listing needs a `read:packages`-scoped token; the UI path above doesn't.)

Until you do this, `docker compose pull` in step 2 will fail — log in with a
PAT that has `read:packages` as a stopgap:

```bash
echo "$GHCR_PAT" | docker login ghcr.io -u <your-github-username> --password-stdin
```

## 1. Bootstrap env file

```bash
cd ~/homelab/containers/yggdrasil
cp yggdrasil.example yggdrasil.env
```

Fill in `yggdrasil.env`. It's a flat file passed via `env_file:` to every
service — docker-compose does **not** cross-substitute `${VAR}` between an
`env_file:` target and the compose YAML, so a few values are intentionally
duplicated under two names (called out inline in the file):
- `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` and `DATABASE_URL`'s embedded password must match.
- `MINIO_ROOT_USER`/`_PASSWORD` and `S3_ACCESS_KEY`/`S3_SECRET_KEY` must match
  (api reads the `S3_*` names).
- `API_PUBLIC_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` must match.

Set:
- `POSTGRES_PASSWORD`, `MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD`/`S3_SECRET_KEY` — any strong
  values (same value in both places per above).
- `SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY` — `openssl rand -base64 32`
- `INTERNAL_API_TOKEN`, `SESSION_SECRET` — `openssl rand -hex 32` each
- `APP_PUBLIC_URL`/`API_PUBLIC_URL`/`DOCS_SITE_URL`/`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`
  — the subdomains you'll create NPM proxy hosts for (suggested:
  `app.smugiwara.com`, `api.smugiwara.com`, `docs.smugiwara.com`)
- `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID`/`GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET` — create a GitHub OAuth App
  (GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App).
  Homepage URL: `APP_PUBLIC_URL`. Authorization callback URL:
  `<API_PUBLIC_URL>/auth/github/callback`. You said you'd handle this
  yourself — do it before first boot, or `GET /auth/github` returns 503.

## 2. Storage dirs + first run

```bash
mkdir -p ~/storage/homelab/homelab-conf/yggdrasil/postgres
mkdir -p ~/storage/homelab/homelab-data/yggdrasil/minio
cd ~/homelab/containers
./up-all-stacks.sh yggdrasil
```

k3s cluster targeting (kubeconfig, ingress class, cert issuer) is configured
entirely in-app now — nothing to bootstrap on the host for it.

## 3. Reverse proxy (nginx-proxy-manager)

Add three proxy hosts in the NPM admin UI (see
`containers/nginx-proxy-manager/.setup` for how to reach it) — plain `http`
scheme to each, HTTP-01 SSL cert like every other stack:

| Domain | Forward to |
|--------|------------|
| `app.smugiwara.com` | `web:3000` |
| `api.smugiwara.com` | `api:3000` |
| `docs.smugiwara.com` | `docusaurus:3000` |

`landing` isn't proxied above — add a fourth host for it (e.g. the bare
`smugiwara.com` or `www.smugiwara.com`) if you want the marketing site
public too; forward to `landing:3000`.

`orchestrator` isn't proxied either — nothing in the web UI calls it
directly from the browser today (the API talks to it over `yggdrasil_net`).
Add a proxy host for `orchestrator:8080` only if/when that changes.

## 4. Verify sign-in

Open `https://app.smugiwara.com`, sign in with GitHub. If `GET /auth/github`
502s or 503s, check `docker compose -f yggdrasil/docker-compose.yml logs api`
— almost always a missing/wrong `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID`/`_SECRET` or callback URL
mismatch.

## Open follow-ups (not done by this setup)

- **GitHub App** (repo access — branches/PRs) — `yggdrasil.env` has the
  `GITHUB_APP_*` vars commented out. Sign-in works without it; the
  Orchestrator can't touch any repo until you create one (GitHub → Settings
  → Developer settings → GitHub Apps → New GitHub App) and uncomment+fill
  those vars.
- **Agent-images** — `SPEC_GRILL_IMAGE`/`FEATURE_BUILD_IMAGE`/`TEST_RUN_IMAGE`
  are commented out in `yggdrasil.env` until `yggdrasil-agent-images`
  actually publishes images. Once it does (and you've made that package
  public per step 0), uncomment and set them, and re-run
  `./up-all-stacks.sh yggdrasil` (orchestrator picks up the new env on
  restart).
- **Reaching a deployed project from outside this host** — not wired up.
  Whatever ingress controller the target cluster runs (where
  `<project-slug>.apps.${APPS_BASE_DOMAIN}` actually lives) isn't published
  anywhere. Decide between a wildcard NPM proxy host (needs DNS-01 wildcard
  cert, unlike every other host here) or a raw host-port carve-out before
  relying on "Open deployment" links in the web UI. See CONTEXT.md.
